WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.664
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:17.295
Unit twenty-seven: Past Perfect Continuous. Today you will explain what had been happening before another past event.

4
00:00:17.595 --> 00:00:20.119
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:24.706
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.412
Had been.

7
00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:30.635
Had been means the helper of the past perfect continuous.

8
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.495
I had been waiting.

9
00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:35.678
Your turn. Say: Had been.

10
00:00:38.533 --> 00:00:39.267
Had been.

11
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:40.902
Duration.

12
00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:44.891
Duration means how long something lasted.

13
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:47.123
The duration was an hour.

14
00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:50.288
Your turn. Say: Duration.

15
00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.134
Duration.

16
00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:55.478
For.

17
00:00:56.483 --> 00:00:58.506
For means with a length of time.

18
00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:00.315
for two hours

19
00:01:00.917 --> 00:01:03.499
Your turn. Say: For.

20
00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:07.056
For.

21
00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:08.806
Since.

22
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:11.839
Since means from a starting point.

23
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.648
since eight

24
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.566
Your turn. Say: Since.

25
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.389
Since.

26
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.314
Before that.

27
00:01:23.317 --> 00:01:25.746
Before that means earlier than a past moment.

28
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.442
Before that, I had been working.

29
00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.470
Your turn. Say: Before that.

30
00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:35.416
Before that.

31
00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.116
Result.

32
00:01:38.117 --> 00:01:40.836
Result means what you can see because of an action.

33
00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.148
The result was tiredness.

34
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.263
Your turn. Say: Result.

35
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:49.997
Result.

36
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:51.658
Ongoing.

37
00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.160
Ongoing means continuing without stopping.

38
00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.239
An ongoing activity.

39
00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.340
Your turn. Say: Ongoing.

40
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.445
Ongoing.

41
00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:06.417
Exhausted.

42
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:09.637
Exhausted means very tired.

43
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.669
I was exhausted.

44
00:02:12.283 --> 00:02:15.145
Your turn. Say: Exhausted.

45
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.071
Exhausted.

46
00:02:19.867 --> 00:02:23.274
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.117 --> 00:02:27.417
Visal, what had you been doing before this lesson started?

48
00:02:28.517 --> 00:02:38.811
I had been revising for twenty minutes. The past perfect continuous is had been plus the -ing form. It shows an action in progress before another past moment.

49
00:02:39.917 --> 00:02:40.953
Why use it?

50
00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:53.514
To explain a past situation: She was exhausted because she had been running. It focuses on the duration or on the visible result of the earlier activity.

51
00:02:54.617 --> 00:02:56.802
How is it different from the past perfect?

52
00:02:57.917 --> 00:03:12.066
The continuous stresses the activity and how long: I had been waiting for an hour. The simple stresses completion: I had waited and then left. State verbs like know do not take the continuous.

53
00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.805
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:20.436
Grammar focus: Past perfect continuous: had been plus verb-ing.

55
00:03:20.736 --> 00:03:21.958
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.940
I had been revising for twenty minutes.

57
00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.163
She was exhausted because she had been running.

58
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:30.829
They had been waiting since eight.

59
00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:38.796
Use had been + verb-ing for an action in progress before another past moment. It explains the cause of a past situation.

60
00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.433
Be careful! Don't say: I was tired because I worked.

61
00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:48.353
Say: I was tired because I had been working.

62
00:03:48.653 --> 00:03:50.281
Use had been + -ing.

63
00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.940
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:55.943
Before That Moment.

65
00:03:56.243 --> 00:03:59.845
Before the lesson started, I had been revising for twenty minutes.

66
00:04:00.833 --> 00:04:03.762
My sister was exhausted because she had been running.

67
00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:07.602
They had been waiting since eight o'clock when the bus came.

68
00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.809
The ground was wet because it had been raining.

69
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.252
The result of the earlier activity was clear.

70
00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:19.159
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:20.017 --> 00:04:22.295
She was tired because she blank all day.

72
00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:26.573
A, had been working. B, has been working. C, worked is.

73
00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:32.319
The answer is A: had been working.

74
00:04:33.483 --> 00:04:36.319
They blank for an hour when it started to rain.

75
00:04:36.619 --> 00:04:40.760
A, had been walking. B, have been walking. C, were walk.

76
00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.346
The answer is A: had been walking.

77
00:04:47.483 --> 00:04:49.053
Which shows duration?

78
00:04:49.353 --> 00:04:53.541
A, had been waiting for an hour. B, had waited. C, waited.

79
00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.785
The answer is A: had been waiting for an hour.

80
00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.056
Which is correct?

81
00:05:02.356 --> 00:05:06.891
A, I had been knowing him.. B, I had known him.. C, I had been know him..

82
00:05:10.433 --> 00:05:12.944
The answer is B: I had known him..

83
00:05:14.083 --> 00:05:17.023
According to the reading, why was the ground wet?

84
00:05:17.323 --> 00:05:22.498
A, it had been raining. B, someone washed it. C, a river flooded.

85
00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:28.648
The answer is A: it had been raining.

86
00:05:29.833 --> 00:05:32.950
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:33.817 --> 00:05:36.223
What had you been doing before this lesson started?

88
00:05:45.017 --> 00:05:46.610
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:59.398
Before this lesson started, I had been revising vocabulary for twenty minutes. I had also been listening to English songs. I use had been plus the -ing form for the earlier activity.

90
00:05:59.698 --> 00:06:01.257
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:08.123
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past perfect continuous: had been plus verb-ing.

92
00:06:08.423 --> 00:06:12.863
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

93
00:06:13.163 --> 00:06:15.827
See you in Unit twenty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:06:16.127 --> 00:06:18.768
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

